{{Quote|Morak? There's nothing on Morak.''"<br />"''It's a secret Imperial mining hub, okay?|Din Djarin and Migs Mayfeld|<ref name="Chapter 15" />}}
'''Morak''' was a [[jungle]] [[planet]] located in [[Wild Space]] on the edge of the [[Outer Rim Territories]] inhabited by [[human]]s as well as [[Shydopp pirates|members]] of the [[Shydopp]] species. The planet served as a secret [[mining]] hub for the [[Galactic Empire]], which processed [[rhydonium]] in a secret [[Morak Imperial refinery|refinery]], which was tightly guarded by [[Coastal defender stormtrooper|shoretroopers]] and [[stormtrooper]]s.

==Description==
Morak was a terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="SWE">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> located in an [[Morak system|eponymous star system]] in [[Wild Space]], situated at the coordinates H-18 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Systems" /> The world featured [[Jungle|rainforests]] and with [[mountain]]s, valleys, and bodies of water.<ref name="Handbook" /> In Morak's ground were meagre deposits of [[rhydonium]], a valuable and highly volatile [[mineral]].<ref name="SWE" /> The world's Type I [[atmosphere]]<ref name="Atmosphere" /> was breathable to at least [[human]]s and [[Shydopp]]s.<ref name="Chapter 15" />

==History==
{{Quote|Empire, New Republic. It's all the same to these people. Invaders on their land is all we are.|Migs Mayfeld to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 15">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 15: The Believer}}</ref>}}
Morak was a largely unknown planet. After the fall of the [[Galactic Empire]], some of its [[Morak Imperial remnants|remnants]] continued to occupy the planet in hopes of rebuilding [[Imperial Military|military forces]]. The Imperial forces there ran a secret [[mining]] operation, extracting rhydonium<ref name="SWE" /> and [[transport]]ing it by [[HCVw A9.2 juggernaut transport]] to an [[Morak Imperial refinery|Imperial refinery]] ran by former [[Imperial officer|officers]] of the Empire's [[Imperial Security Bureau]].<ref name="Chapter 15" /> [[Valin Hess]], an Imperial [[general]], was also present at the refinery.<ref name="Handbook" /> As Morak was outside the jurisdiction of the [[New Republic]], which controlled much of [[the galaxy]], the [[Politics|government]] largely ignored the Imperial presence there.<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> However, a group of [[Homeworld|native]] [[Shydopp pirates]] fought against the Imperial presence there.<ref name="Handbook" />

In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> a [[mercenary]] group led by the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]] [[Mission to Morak|travelled]] to Morak, intending to use an Imperial terminal to locate the [[Gideon's light cruiser|cruiser]] of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]. They were led there by [[Migs Mayfeld]], a former Imperial [[Sniper|sharpshooter]] [[Migs Mayfeld]] who had formerly served under Hess.<ref name="Chapter 15" />

In their escape, Mayfeld fired [[Boba Fett]]'s [[cycler rifle]] at the shipment of rhydonium, setting off an explosion that destroyed the refinery. During the destruction of the refinery, there were multiple [[Imperial officer]]s and other Imperial persons present, including Mayfeld's previous commanding officer [[Valin Hess]], whom Mayfeld shot shortly before the refinery exploded.<ref name="Chapter 15" />

